WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.467
Luke, Chapter Seven.

2
00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:07.600
Now when he had ended all his sayings in the audience of the people, he entered into Capernaum.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.600
And a certain centurion's servant, who was dear unto him, was sick, and ready to die.

4
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:20.667
And when he heard of Jesus, he sent unto him the elders of the Jews, beseeching him that he would come and heal his servant.

5
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:30.933
And when they came to Jesus, they besought him instantly, saying, That he was worthy for whom he should do this: For he loveth our nation, and he hath built us a synagogue.

6
00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:33.067
Then Jesus went with them.

7
00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:52.933
And when he was now not far from the house, the centurion sent friends to him, saying unto him, Lord, trouble not thyself: for I am not worthy that thou shouldest enter under my roof: Wherefore neither thought I myself worthy to come unto thee: but say in a word, and my servant shall be healed.

8
00:00:52.933 --> 00:01:06.267
For I also am a man set under authority, having under me soldiers, and I say unto one, Go, and he goeth; and to another, Come, and he cometh; and to my servant, Do this, and he doeth it.

9
00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:16.800
When Jesus heard these things, he marvelled at him, and turned him about, and said unto the people that followed him, I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel.

10
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.600
And they that were sent, returning to the house, found the servant whole that had been sick.

11
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:29.200
And it came to pass the day after, that he went into a city called Nain; and many of his disciples went with him, and much people.

12
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:39.333
Now when he came nigh to the gate of the city, behold, there was a dead man carried out, the only son of his mother, and she was a widow: and much people of the city was with her.

13
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:44.533
And when the Lord saw her, he had compassion on her, and said unto her, Weep not.

14
00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:48.800
And he came and touched the bier: and they that bare him stood still.

15
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.000
And he said, Young man, I say unto thee, Arise.

16
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.333
And he that was dead sat up, and began to speak.

17
00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:57.733
And he delivered him to his mother.

18
00:01:57.733 --> 00:02:07.067
And there came a fear on all: and they glorified God, saying, That a great prophet is risen up among us; and, That God hath visited his people.

19
00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:12.933
And this rumour of him went forth throughout all Judaea, and throughout all the region round about.

20
00:02:12.933 --> 00:02:16.133
And the disciples of John shewed him of all these things.

21
00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:22.000
And John calling unto him two of his disciples sent them to Jesus, saying, Art thou he that should come?

22
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.133
or look we for another?

23
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:30.667
When the men were come unto him, they said, John Baptist hath sent us unto thee, saying, Art thou he that should come?

24
00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.000
or look we for another?

25
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:40.000
And in that same hour he cured many of their infirmities and plagues, and of evil spirits; and unto many that were blind he gave sight.

26
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:54.133
Then Jesus answering said unto them, Go your way, and tell John what things ye have seen and heard; how that the blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, to the poor the gospel is preached.

27
00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:58.267
And blessed is he, whosoever shall not be offended in me.

28
00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:06.933
And when the messengers of John were departed, he began to speak unto the people concerning John, What went ye out into the wilderness for to see?

29
00:03:06.933 --> 00:03:08.800
A reed shaken with the wind?

30
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.200
But what went ye out for to see?

31
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.200
A man clothed in soft raiment?

32
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.200
Behold, they which are gorgeously apparelled, and live delicately, are in kings' courts.

33
00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.000
But what went ye out for to see?

34
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:22.800
A prophet?

35
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.400
Yea, I say unto you, and much more than a prophet.

36
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:34.133
This is he, of whom it is written, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee.

37
00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:43.600
For I say unto you, Among those that are born of women there is not a greater prophet than John the Baptist: but he that is least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.

38
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:49.867
And all the people that heard him, and the publicans, justified God, being baptized with the baptism of John.

39
00:03:49.867 --> 00:03:55.467
But the Pharisees and lawyers rejected the counsel of God against themselves, being not baptized of him.

40
00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:59.333
And the Lord said, Whereunto then shall I liken the men of this generation?

41
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:01.200
and to what are they like?

42
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:13.467
They are like unto children sitting in the marketplace, and calling one to another, and saying, We have piped unto you, and ye have not danced; we have mourned to you, and ye have not wept.

43
00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:20.800
For John the Baptist came neither eating bread nor drinking wine; and ye say, He hath a devil.

44
00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:30.000
The Son of man is come eating and drinking; and ye say, Behold a gluttonous man, and a winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners!

45
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.800
But wisdom is justified of all her children.

46
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.267
And one of the Pharisees desired him that he would eat with him.

47
00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:40.133
And he went into the Pharisee's house, and sat down to meat.

48
00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:57.467
And, behold, a woman in the city, which was a sinner, when she knew that Jesus sat at meat in the Pharisee's house, brought an alabaster box of ointment, And stood at his feet behind him weeping, and began to wash his feet with tears, and did wipe them with the hairs of her head,

49
00:04:57.467 --> 00:05:00.667
and kissed his feet, and anointed them with the ointment.

50
00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:13.067
Now when the Pharisee which had bidden him saw it, he spake within himself, saying, This man, if he were a prophet, would have known who and what manner of woman this is that toucheth him: for she is a sinner.

51
00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:18.533
And Jesus answering said unto him, Simon, I have somewhat to say unto thee.

52
00:05:18.533 --> 00:05:20.933
And he saith, Master, say on.

53
00:05:20.933 --> 00:05:26.667
There was a certain creditor which had two debtors: the one owed five hundred pence, and the other fifty.

54
00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:30.667
And when they had nothing to pay, he frankly forgave them both.

55
00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:34.533
Tell me therefore, which of them will love him most?

56
00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:39.200
Simon answered and said, I suppose that he, to whom he forgave most.

57
00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.267
And he said unto him, Thou hast rightly judged.

58
00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:46.933
And he turned to the woman, and said unto Simon, Seest thou this woman?

59
00:05:46.933 --> 00:05:55.200
I entered into thine house, thou gavest me no water for my feet: but she hath washed my feet with tears, and wiped them with the hairs of her head.

60
00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.933
Thou gavest me no kiss: but this woman since the time I came in hath not ceased to kiss my feet.

61
00:06:00.933 --> 00:06:06.133
My head with oil thou didst not anoint: but this woman hath anointed my feet with ointment.

62
00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:14.933
Wherefore I say unto thee, Her sins, which are many, are forgiven; for she loved much: but to whom little is forgiven, the same loveth little.

63
00:06:14.933 --> 00:06:17.867
And he said unto her, Thy sins are forgiven.

64
00:06:17.867 --> 00:06:24.400
And they that sat at meat with him began to say within themselves, Who is this that forgiveth sins also?

65
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.667
And he said to the woman, Thy faith hath saved thee; go in peace.

